A=\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 & -1 \\ 7 & -2 & 4 \\ 0 & 5 & 6\end{bmatrix},\,B=\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 \\ -5 & 18 & 4 \\ -18 & 35 & 6\end{bmatrix}
$$

By applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?"] [:db/add "c7c550fa-a627-5c43-bc1d-dd6031afbf62" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left of $a_{13}=-1$ equal to $0.$

To do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:

$$
\begin{aligned}A &=\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 & -1 \\ 7 & -2 & 4 \\ 0 & 5 & 6\end{bmatrix}
\\ &\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-3C_{3}}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -1 \\ -5 & -2 & 4 \\ -18 & 5 & 6\end{bmatrix}
\\ &\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+5C_{3}}\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -1 \\ -5 & 18 & 4 \\ -18 & 35 & 6\end{bmatrix}\\ &=B\end{aligned}
$$

